+# Marginalia Books
+
+A website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop. It has four pages (home, books, events and visit), a genre-filtered catalogue, an events list and a contact form.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step, no package to install and no external requests: no CDNs, web fonts, analytics or remote images.
+
+## Run it
+
+Either open `index.html` directly in a browser, or serve the folder from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then visit http://localhost:8000/.
+
+The contact form is a demo. It validates input in the browser and says plainly that nothing was sent; it does not submit anywhere.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the shared stylesheet.
+- `js/books.js`: genre filter, with the selected genre kept in the URL (`books.html?genre=mystery`).
+- `js/visit.js`: contact form validation.
+- `tests/run.mjs`: browser tests.
+
+## Tests
+
+The tests use Playwright from a global npm install and a Chrome binary. They start a local server on a random port, load each page in headless Chrome, and fail on any console error or any request to another origin.
+
+```sh
+node tests/run.mjs
+```
+
+Pass a name fragment to run a subset, for example `node tests/run.mjs books`. The script exits non-zero if any test fails.
+
+If the Playwright bundled browser is not installed, the tests fall back to `/usr/bin/google-chrome`.
